# std/diff — one of the history tools (std/git-history holds the source they share).
# The help is a HERE-STRING so it lives in this expression, which is stripped
# from the tree the build sees: editing the docs re-keys this tool's ArgTree and
# nothing it builds from.
HELP=<<END
Unified diff between two revisions of a source tree, optionally scoped to a path. `root` is the source tree, such as sources/repo/02-layer. Defaults compare the previous commit to the source tree's own (what the latest step changed). `from` and `to` accept a commit hash, or HEAD with ~N or ^ ancestry. To compare with another source tree (such as sources/repo/00-base, for a layer's whole change), name it as `against`.
@param [from] The base revision (default HEAD~1, the commit before the source tree's own).
@param [to] The revision to compare against the base (default HEAD, the source tree's own commit).
@param {commit} [against] Another source tree in the session, or a commit hash, to use as the base instead of `from`.
@param [path] Restrict the diff to this source-tree-relative path.
@root
END
IMAGE=run --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/rustc --src:@=DEEP-DEPS/git-history --dep0:@=DEEP-DEPS/session-protocol --dep1:@=DEEP-DEPS/git-locator --output-runner:@=DEEP-DEPS/git-runner
curry --base=$IMAGE --op=diff --help=$HELP
